## 1. 30-day roadmap — one topic per day

### Phase 1 — Dev communication foundations (Days 1–7)

| Day | Topic | Why it matters |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **1** | Daily standup | Most frequent 2-min English moment in a dev's week |
| **2** | Explaining a bug | Core collaboration skill — root cause + fix + impact |
| **3** | Code review comments | Give and receive feedback without sounding rude |
| **4** | Thinking phrases (buy time) | Stop awkward silences; replace Vietnamese "ờ… à…" |
| **5** | Linking words | Sound structured, not choppy — connect ideas like a senior |
| **6** | Softening language | Disagree / push back without offending |
| **7** | STAR storytelling — intro | Base pattern for every interview answer |

### Phase 2 — Technical fluency (Days 8–14)

| Day | Topic |
| --- | --- |
| **8** | Explaining trade-offs (X vs Y — Redux vs Query, REST vs GraphQL) |
| **9** | Describing architecture out loud (feature folders, boundaries) |
| **10** | Performance discussion (profiler, measurements, before/after) |
| **11** | API / integration issues (401s, timeouts, retries, contracts) |
| **12** | State management explanation (server vs client, cache, invalidation) |
| **13** | Async flows, race conditions, offline (describing failure modes) |
| **14** | Week 2 review + tech story drill (record yourself) |

### Phase 3 — Interview core (Days 15–21)

| Day | Topic |
| --- | --- |
| **15** | STAR — proudest project story (with a metric) |
| **16** | STAR — conflict with a teammate |
| **17** | STAR — failure and lesson learned |
| **18** | System design intro (mobile scope): auth, lists, errors |
| **19** | System design — caching, offline, push notifications |
| **20** | Coding interview narration (think-aloud while solving) |
| **21** | "Tell me about yourself" + 60-second career pitch |

### Phase 4 — Senior-level communication (Days 22–30)

| Day | Topic |
| --- | --- |
| **22** | Handling pushback (PM wants impossible deadline; engineer disagrees) |
| **23** | Leading a meeting / discussion (open, guide, close) |
| **24** | Writing vs speaking: Slack updates, PR descriptions, Jira comments |
| **25** | Explaining incidents & on-call (timeline + root cause + mitigation) |
| **26** | Mentoring / giving feedback to a junior |
| **27** | Negotiating scope / deadlines (not "no", but "yes if…") |
| **28** | Cross-functional (talking to design, backend, QA — different vocab) |
| **29** | Full mock interview (behavioral + technical + coding narration) |
| **30** | Career story wrap-up + final self-assessment + next 30-day plan |

