## 4. Linker progression map (cross-day spaced repetition)

Linking words + fillers are **not** crammed into a single day. They are distributed across 7 days + drilled again in a second day for spaced repetition. Full reference lives in **`english-linkers.mdc`** (on-demand).

| Group (see `english-linkers.mdc`) | Introduce on | Drill again on | Why this pairing |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **1. Conditional / IF-type** (otherwise, in case, as long as, even if) | Day 11 (API / integration) | Day 25 (incidents) | Error handling language naturally uses conditionals |
| **2. Contrast** (however, though, still, on the other hand) | Day 5 (linkers core) | Day 14 (week review) | Structured disagreement / trade-offs |
| **3. Addition** (also, as well, besides, in addition, plus) | Day 5 (linkers core) | Day 14 | Stack multiple points in one update |
| **4. Cause / Result** (because, since, so, that's why, therefore) | Day 5 (linkers core) | Day 14 | Root cause explanation backbone |
| **5. Examples / Explanation** (for example, such as, like, in other words) | Day 2 (explaining bugs) | Day 18 (system design) | Concrete examples = senior habit |
| **6. Time / Sequence** (first, then, while, meanwhile, eventually) | Day 1 (standup) | Day 25 (incident timeline) | Both are time-ordered narratives |
| **7. Emphasis** (actually, basically, honestly) | Day 4 (thinking phrases) | Day 21 (career pitch) | Sincerity markers during storytelling |
| **8. Fillers** (well, you know, I mean, kind of, right?) | Day 4 (thinking phrases) | Day 29 (mock interview) | Fillers = pressure tested best in interview sim |
| **9. Conclusion / Closing** (so, anyway, in the end, at the end of the day, to wrap up) | Day 23 (leading meeting) | Day 30 (wrap-up) | Meeting closers + career story closers |

**AI behavior:** when generating any of these days, AI must:

1. Open `english-linkers.mdc` and pull **only the relevant group** into that day's Section 1.2.
2. Add a short note like *"Today's linker focus: Group 6 — Time / Sequence. Full reference: `english-linkers.mdc`."*
3. On drill-again days, pull the group(s) from the drill-again column and design a **pressure scenario** that forces their use.

