## 6. Daily principles (senior habits applied to language)

- **Tie every phrase to a real work moment.** If I can't imagine using it this week, cut it.
- **Shadow before composing.** Repetition → fluency → own voice.
- **Record once per week** (Day 7, 14, 21, 30) — compare, hear the progress.
- **Own 1–3 phrases per day** I could use at tomorrow's standup without thinking.
- **Correct once, move on.** Don't obsess over perfection; senior comm is **clear enough, fast enough**.

